#
# Conformance case: teleology/serial-conjunction-split.
#
# A logic:SerialConjunction (φ ⊗ ψ) is executed under executional entailment from a
# start state. φ (stepOne) requires `initialized` and asserts `stepOneDone`; ψ (stepTwo)
# requires `stepOneDone` and asserts `stepTwoDone`. The path SPLITS: φ runs over the
# prefix (s0 → s1), then ψ runs over the suffix (s1 → s2), the split point forced to φ's
# end state. The engine records a logic:TransactionOutcome with logic:transactionSucceeds
# true, the executed logic:Path (s0 → s1 → s2 via logic:temporallySucceeds), and the
# per-step support as supersession. Proves serial-conjunction path-splitting.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/serial-conjunction-split/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
